  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x35F" flags="0x0">
    <title>KFNWKRE @ 0x1CDA2C</title>
    <description>Intake cam target used under knock control (Bosch: desired cam angle for detonation, inlet). Weighted in when knock retard is active (wnwskwke_w). Stock: much less advance than KFNWSE at 1000-1500 rpm mid load, and -7 (more advance) instead of +10 at 6000 rpm full load. Code-referenced at 0x1448A0. Angle convention: degrees crank relative to gas-exchange TDC; intake reference (parked) position WNWREO = 27.0, intake fully advanced limit WNWSMNE = -23.0; exhaust reference WNWRAS = 26.5, limit WNWSMNA = -3.5. Lower number = cam advanced. Load axis tops out at 131 percent, so all boost loads use the last column.</description>
