  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x361" flags="0x0">
    <title>KFNWSE @ 0x1CDB5E</title>
    <description>Intake cam target, warm engine, normal running (Bosch: nominal angle of camshaft, general conditions, intake). CONFIRMED IN CODE 2026-11-18: read by the 16-bit group-map routine 0x10B150 at 0x144BD0 with the rpm axis SNM16NEUW (0x1CDF2A) and the load axis rlnw_w (0x1CDF76); result stored to RAM 0x8036B0 = wnwshwe_w (desired intake cam, homogeneous mode, warm engine) - the Ford RAM name and the Ford map name agree. Then blended with KFNWWLE (warm-up, by temperature factor KFNWTME), KFNWKRE (knock) and the idle/cat-heating maps into wnwse_w (0x7FAB0A, logged from 2026-11-18). LOG CHECK PENDING: compare wnwse_w with this map on a warm log. Angle convention: degrees crank relative to gas-exchange TDC; intake reference (parked) position WNWREO = 27.0, intake fully advanced limit WNWSMNE = -23.0; exhaust reference WNWRAS = 26.5, limit WNWSMNA = -3.5. Lower number = cam advanced. Load axis tops out at 131 percent, so all boost loads use the last column.</description>
