  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x4E5" flags="0x0">
    <title>FRLFSDP @ 0x1D279E</title>
    <description>Multiplier on the injector constant vs fuel pressure minus manifold pressure (dppk_w, RAM 0x803DD4, 0.3125 hPa per bit). Bosch name FRLFSDP (injection correction for RLFS) from the Ford A2L (Ford 0x1D2D06, scaling raw/32768 confirmed). Code 0x14747C-0x14749C: 16-bit curve, header 0x1D2786 (n = 11), axis 0x1D2788, values 0x1D279E (1.0 = 32768). frkate_w = this x KLFUDENS x injector constant (0x1D27B6). Stock: 1.495 at 170 kPa, 1.143 at 280, 1.057 at 340, 0.975 at 400, 0.934 at 520 kPa difference (close to the square-root law up to 400 kPa). LOG CHECK 2026-11-18: injection time per percent of fuel load rises 40 percent as the pressure difference falls from 367 to 244 kPa; with this curve and FKKVS applied it is constant within about 2 percent (0.087-0.090 ms per percent) from 30 to 170 percent load.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <units>index</units>
      <indexcount>1</indexcount>
      <outputtype>4</outputtype>
      <LABEL index="0" value="0" />
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1D2788" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>kPa diff</units>
      <indexcount>11</indexcount>
      <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X*0.03125">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="z">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x00" mmedaddress="0x1D279E" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedrowcount="11" mmedcolcount="1" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>factor</units>
      <decimalpl>3</decimalpl>
      <outputtype>1</outputtype>
      <MATH equation="X/32768">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFTABLE>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x4E6" flags="0x0">
    <title>KRKATE @ 0x1D27B6</title>
    <description>Injection time per percent of relative fuel mass at the reference pressure difference (about 382 kPa) and normal fuel temperature. Bosch name KRKATE (conversion from relative fuel mass rk into effective injection time te) from the Ford A2L (Ford 0x1D2D36); A2L scaling raw/96000 ms per percent = the same as derived from code. Ford RS value 6973 (= 0.0726, about 18 percent bigger injectors). Code 0x1474BC: frkate_w (RAM 0x7FADAA) = pressure curve x density x this value / 2^17; tef = rk_w x frkate_w / 2^9 x FKKVS. Stock raw 8261 = 0.0861 ms per percent. CONFIRMED BY LOGS 2026-11-18: measured 0.087-0.090 ms per percent across 30-170 percent load (the 1-4 percent difference = fuel trims and wall film). Scale 1/96000 ms per percent per bit (code and A2L agree). Raising it = bigger injectors in the ECU model: richer everywhere. Not needed for the stock injectors.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1D27B6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>ms/%</units>
    <decimalpl>5</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X*0.0000104167">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
